#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119599 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119788 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fcf3704-4856-5095-a6f4-7ec20d81f3c4" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing an Unknown in Terms of 2x2 Determinants"}] :question/id #uuid "4efedc4e-19e9-552c-bc27-814df953e141" :question/math-academy-id "e-4575" :question/problem "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+2y &=-1 \\\\ -3x+3y &=9.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nExpress $y$ in terms of $2 \\times 2$ determinants." :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+2y &=-1 \\\\ -3x+3y &=9.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct $D_y$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119601 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119790 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9b0f65-d8a3-57c4-88c5-2738b0938c0d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "311ba12f-de22-580c-9e0d-6766f7864d1a" :question/math-academy-id "e-4578" :question/problem "Let $\\langle x,3 \\rangle$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-2y &=4 \\\\ x+ky &=8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\nI. ![](images/7d/7d767f03d04f1c35a774ef089d706894b2fe426995f1c7c050f8c5af0ef9e1e2.svg)\n\nII. ![](images/5a/5a9fe2dde8c8202f4532f745f0fac58ec649bdf39e928560ccaa2485d0f6f09e.svg)\n\nIII. ![](images/7e/7e2a9ca703f25107de026c84a8e7feb6099b48c7794ffdc166108358701feb8f.svg)" :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\dfrac{D_y}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5\\cdot 8-4\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{36}{|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{aligned}| & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119658 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119844 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7580024-f357-57d4-94f2-85c25e2c144b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Parts of Cramer's Rule Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "d81e32a1-bd93-5a95-bb4a-e8df9063b5aa" :question/math-academy-id "e-5230" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y &=2 \\\\ 2x+y &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $x$ can be written as\n![](images/f5/f5c9b1c83ed648b56b47bd370ba5b15359521492087eda769d4122be99384a0f.svg)\nExpress $D_x$ in terms of a $2 \\times 2$ determinant." :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y &=2 \\\\ 2x+y &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct $D_x$, we replace the first column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388632 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119788 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fcf3704-4856-5095-a6f4-7ec20d81f3c4" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing an Unknown in Terms of 2x2 Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81a9c740-e176-5d4f-b580-d90c73c50672" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -14 \\\\ 5 & 13\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388634} {:answer/id #uuid "7ad108c0-dc3e-5d9f-bd6c-a73cc3fbf1cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -14 \\\\ 5 & 13\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}8 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388635} {:answer/id #uuid "efc33b0f-b9f4-5215-ae08-da3aa1c28f48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ 5 & 17\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388636} {:answer/id #uuid "b5c4f737-0790-54cf-88d7-2c95fda98258" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 2 \\\\ 13 & 5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388637} {:answer/id #uuid "1b3a1b35-f59f-515b-b7d3-68b5c1ed8ad4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 2 \\\\ 13 & 5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}8 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81a9c740-e176-5d4f-b580-d90c73c50672" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -14 \\\\ 5 & 13\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388634} :answer-field/id #uuid "46a433c9-a1b6-5e55-9a26-b5a8790a2ae4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388633}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3dee3a3d-b589-52d5-8b29-2264540bb947" :question/math-academy-id "q-139960" :question/problem "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+8y &=-14 \\\\ 5x+4y &=13.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $y=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+8y &=-14 \\\\ 5x+4y &=13.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$ we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -14 \\\\ 5 & 13\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -14 \\\\ 5 & 13\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186271991 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119790 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9b0f65-d8a3-57c4-88c5-2738b0938c0d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8504eb0f-93c6-5d20-8195-88dbad00b315" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464078} {:answer/id #uuid "c70ffc2d-dbef-5e28-8e5a-6e4a97b209b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident