/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477324}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1ecface-1c0b-5ded-a848-6fd964ffc91d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477323} :answer-field/id #uuid "117e65ce-2b43-5f0f-aeab-5d34d9cf7493" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477631}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "38525400-a144-5244-a7f9-f068d294beba" :question/math-academy-id "q-42983" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,3⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y &=10 \\\\ kx-4y &=12.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\nI. $3|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ k & -4\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ k & 12\\end{aligned}|$\n\nII. $|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ k & -4\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ k & 12\\end{aligned}|$\n\nIII. $|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ k & -4\\end{aligned}|=3|\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ k & 12\\end{aligned}|$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ k & -4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ k & 12\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ k & 12\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ k & -4\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ 3|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ k & -4\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ k & 12\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338748 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119788 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fcf3704-4856-5095-a6f4-7ec20d81f3c4" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing an Unknown in Terms of 2x2 Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5724c9ae-dc06-5f04-a7bb-16c79f89623e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}21 & 5 \\\\ 12 & 2\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336831} {:answer/id #uuid "79aa5121-234b-5948-84ff-1f6f15cbba44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 12 \\\\ 21 & 5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337126} {:answer/id #uuid "c1ea90dc-0d02-5398-9ad2-067e1cf603ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 12 \\\\ 4 & 21\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337756} {:answer/id #uuid "e5721947-bbab-5d0d-9e98-e795547ab7a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 21 \\\\ 3 & 12\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338034} {:answer/id #uuid "f242b257-2ab8-51b4-b202-dfd535c14a05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}12 & 2 \\\\ 21 & 5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338152}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f242b257-2ab8-51b4-b202-dfd535c14a05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}12 & 2 \\\\ 21 & 5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338152} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4bf4df1-eabd-54c5-9df4-7454b683ca46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338609}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "04beac6b-a557-5165-adec-a531623a11c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-70106" :question/problem "Consider the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y &=12 \\\\ 4x+5y &=21.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $x=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y &=12 \\\\ 4x+5y &=21.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we construct ${D}_{x}$, we replace the first column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}12 & 2 \\\\ 21 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}12 & 2 \\\\ 21 & 5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553569 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119788 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fcf3704-4856-5095-a6f4-7ec20d81f3c4" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing an Unknown in Terms of 2x2 Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10c31cbf-e411-5a16-8126-ed9a704efadf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 7 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552892} {:answer/id #uuid "1c419977-a9db-50ee-ad18-ae9235af700f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}7 & -4 \\\\ -8 & -2\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552919} {:answer/id #uuid "3830ad06-0fa6-5789-b242-ad71e1909f24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}5 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552980} {:answer/id #uuid "9cdc06c8-14af-5ae9-b49d-c138304f6741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -8\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553188} {:answer/id #uuid "cc42aca7-24ec-5837-8d84-2adcce5421a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 \\\\ 5 & -8\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc42aca7-24ec-5837-8d84-2adcce5421a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 \\\\ 5 & -8\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553277} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b06cb65-9120-515c-8370-2f1d8ca0a88e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553412}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c0707c67-e191-5de9-a1ec-b2b0c2ac11dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-70107" :question/problem "Consider the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-4y=7 \\\\ 5x-2y=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $y=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-4y=7 \\\\ 5x-2y=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$ we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 \\\\ 5 & -8\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 \\\\ 5 & -8\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393681 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119788 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fcf3704-4856-5095-a6f4-7ec20d81f3c4" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing an Unknown in Terms of 2x2 Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "447eaab9-6da2-5044-99db-4a1a4223532f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393683} {:answer/id #uuid "78a86f8d-aae4-5a4d-95e4-fab946aebfd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393684} {:answer/id #uuid "38a07045-f8ae-5e87-9321-f64593af7a55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393685} {:answer/id #uuid "e48114b7-c325-58ff-8779-f2b138d44c14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393686} {:answer/id #uuid "19c2ae1c-bf55-56a8-9095-d30b83511f64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38a07045-f8ae-5e87-9321-f64593af7a55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393685} :answer-field/id #uuid "87423d6e-0ff7-5bbe-8eda-f375b8d4efa0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393682}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "94153e84-a333-5aec-b75c-49c1a118f48c" :question/math-academy-id "q-77398" :question/problem "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+2y &=5 \\\\ x-3y &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $y=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+2y &=5 \\\\ x-3y &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$ we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345293 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119790 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9b0f65-d8a3-57c4-88c5-2738b0938c0d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7a2c945-cc7a-516f-b667-0d89251d3b88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468196} {:answer/id #uuid "40dd3909-7386-578c-83fe-14ada120188c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40dd3909-7386-578c-83fe-14ada120188c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468197} :answer-field/id #uuid "a689391a-097b-5af2-9f28-47cb333ebeda" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468819} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd7b34da-0847-5b45-af70-c9c06b31eade" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468198} {:answer/id #uuid "a7025902-02fe-5c8c-8871-b5a8b672cf56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd7b34da-0847-5b45-af70-c9c06b31eade" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468198} :answer-field/id #uuid "55fe37fb-e330-5dc6-9f1e-3cb5a382485e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468820} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f36311c-d5c2-569b-97ab-eaf35ae46749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468200} {:answer/id #uuid "4903bf3a-5ec0-502a-9315-987f705aa1f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f36311c-d5c2-569b-97ab-eaf35ae46749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468200} :answer-field/id #uuid "efa69594-ec70-57b1-b89f-3696a43adfec" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468821}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dfe3c702-6424-5bb5-8a56-52b5a6e22724" :question/math-academy-id "q-77400" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,-2⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y &=2 \\\\ 2x+y &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n- **I.** $|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}|=-6$\n- **II.** $|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}|=-12$\n- **III.** $|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}|=3$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1+2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D} \\\\ -2 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}|}{3} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}| & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345294 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119790 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9b0f65-d8a3-57c4-88c5-2738b0938c0d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d68061f9-26f7-5cb1-b451-9613d07f582b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468202} {:answer/id #uuid "305d62c3-fb2c-554a-888b-993e673cc358" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d68061f9-26f7-5cb1-b451-9613d07f582b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468202} :answer-field/id #uuid "7204a3ea-ab6b-5c40-bbe8-ec855216acb2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468822} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29506dd5-d859-5ad5-9d4b-430345bd390d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468204} {:answer/id #uuid "8aa20fab-5c90-5c84-a527-307ae07a2504" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29506dd5-d859-5ad5-9d4b-430345bd390d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468204} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ae3e59d-3a9b-58cd-9548-f87659ec9274" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468823} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db9a7f34-a705-56e4-95cf-26717aba6aa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468206} {:answer/id #uuid "b87a5642-b55a-55d3-b69c-559ebce5dc2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b87a5642-b55a-55d3-b69c-559ebce5dc2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468207} :answer-field/id #uuid "f473da0d-0013-52fe-bd69-e5c67cc3e1ac" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468824}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a75a54e5-59f0-5536-9005-ac12974e1a69" :question/math-academy-id "q-77401" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,1⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-y &=k \\\\ x+4y &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n- **I.** $|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|=5$\n- **II.** $|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|=-7$\n- **III.** $|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|=13$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =12+1 \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|}{13} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441147 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119790 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9b0f65-d8a3-57c4-88c5-2738b0938c0d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13abba68-c603-520c-b95e-bae74246f467" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441124} {:answer/id #uuid "37e0bd1c-a3ae-5f52-a82d-3a71181d02f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441127} {:answer/id #uuid "45f349a4-8a10-5b19-b4f8-85a49af13560" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441129} {:answer/id #uuid "8d3a2a97-810a-5f83-ae72-fc21a76e36d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441132} {:answer/id #uuid "ed90928a-c1d1-55de-ac12-d5f61d39fd02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37e0bd1c-a3ae-5f52-a82d-3a71181d02f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441127} :answer-field/id #uuid "1aec48af-7f8c-53fd-bb3d-101ace543e43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441144}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1485a2c5-d3d5-5ae7-bfda-a8f34f74aef0" :question/math-academy-id "q-77402" :question/problem "Let $⟨2,y⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+ky &=5 \\\\ x+2y &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\nI. $|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|$\n\nII. $2|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|$\n\nIII. $|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=2|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|$" :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ 2|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}]}
